# TitanGold Core Engineering Rules v4.7

## Outcome-Driven, Risk-Based Vertical Slice, Source-of-Truth, Secure Integration, Production Verification and Human-QA Standard

These rules are mandatory for all TitanGold engineering work.

They replace TitanGold Core Engineering Rules v4.6.

They preserve the strict security, runtime-safety, Source-of-Truth, deployment,
Git, Human-QA, Agent-productization, evidence-validity, CI-differential and
delivery-lifecycle standards of v4.6 while preserving the canonical Agent-to-Artemis
architecture, role boundaries, evidence contracts, cross-Agent compatibility,
decision lineage, evaluation and automated-trading maturity rules and adding the
Artemis 15-stage Core Completion roadmap, canonical Settings/API-integration
ownership, multi-provider AI advisory Council, task-aware model routing, memory,
advisor-performance evaluation, continuous-learning governance and measured
self-sufficiency rules required for TitanGold's long-term central intelligence,
while adding the canonical Artemis cognitive identity, Decision Context,
Cognitive Kernel, deterministic-versus-model-assisted reasoning boundary,
model-independence rules, canonical Artemis Decision artifact, explicit
Cognitive-Decision-versus-Execution-Authorization semantics and cognitive
failure/evaluation gates required for Artemis to operate as a real central AI
system rather than a wrapper around any single LLM.

Cursor must follow these rules silently and consistently throughout the
project.

