# 4. Work-Package Types

Every task must be classified as one of the following.

## 4.1 Read-Only Discovery

Purpose:

- Inspect architecture
- Reproduce defects
- Map dependencies
- Verify Sources of Truth
- Produce an implementation plan

No mutation is allowed.

## 4.2 Outcome Vertical Slice

The default implementation unit.

It completes one useful workflow across all affected layers.

## 4.3 Program Slice

Used for a large end-to-end product capability that cannot be made useful
through artificial micro-slices.

A Program Slice may include internal phases such as:

- Discovery
- Foundation
- Backend contract
- Provider integration
- Frontend workflow
- Capability mapping
- Security hardening
- Browser QA
- Human QA
- Closeout

Internal phases do not automatically require separate user approval,
separate Dynamic Rules or separate Human-QA cycles.

The Program Slice must still have one primary outcome, one Source-of-Truth
model and explicit high-risk gates.

Examples:

- MEXC End-to-End Connection Platform
- Wallet Deposit/Withdrawal/Transfer Workflow
- Complete Arbitrage Agent
- Futures Trading Foundation

## 4.4 Shared Foundation Work Package

Used only for a proven cross-cutting defect or a new shared capability needed
by multiple consumers.

## 4.5 Remediation Bundle

Used when Human QA or Browser QA finds multiple related low- or medium-risk
defects inside the same approved outcome.

Related defects should be fixed together when they share the same workflow or
acceptance criteria.

Do not create a new micro-slice for every button, label or spacing defect.

## 4.6 Documentation-Only Closeout

Used only after implementation and Human QA are complete.

It must not pretend that runtime code changed.

